    "q-122813": {
      "dom_id": "step-q122813",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14114615/assets/50bd80ab9aa2f8d5ac2a453ccfe63815a75379efa7502cf1090eb015264206f6.png)\n\nThe gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)$ is shown above. Which of the following could be a contour plot of $f(x,y)?$",
      "worked_solution": "The gradient field vectors of a function $f(x,y)$ always lie perpendicular to its level curves.\n\nObserve that the given field vectors are perpendicular to the level curves in the following picture.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14114615/assets/b73b05cb7f58bcce1d684c7f19c391ecd2033eb4c47c59daf896546956a9d42f.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14114615/assets/b8b4cae5128667b4a75097540bddc8dbb853744aee65e96204cf630ccb30fc68.png)",
